{+Climb batch 7's rung H (`952892a00`) cleared those 18 (`compile-ladder/rung-exclusion-remainder/REPORT.md` sections 4 to 9): `TotalComparison` extends `Comparison` alone, as the compiler prelude's does (`ProjectFortress/LibraryBuiltin/CompilerBuiltin.fsi:719-722`), and extends no order, as the specification's does, whose supertypes are `Comparison` and the three traits of `LEXICO`'s algebra (`Specification/advanced-lib/comparison.tex:28-32`), restating `>=`, `<=`, `MIN`, `MAX` and `MINMAX` at itself with `StandardTotalOrder`'s bodies (`Library/FortressLibrary.fss:170-175`); `AnyMaybe` extends `AnyUniqueItem` alone and writes the `opr =` its api declares (`.fss:1400-1403`); `RelationalPredicateCondition[\E\]` no longer excludes its own supertype, its component-only second `ANDCOND` renamed `andRelCond` and chosen by a `typecase` in `andCondCombine` at `FilterGenerator2`'s two call sites (`.fss:4514`, `:4516`, `:4556-4566`), zero.md's P3d with the two changes the compiled checker needs. The cost: a program's own `p1 ANDCOND p2` of two relational predicates is no longer relational under walk, while `filter` keeps the fusion (row 458). On the flat library the checker now reports no exclusion error (`compile-ladder/rung-exclusion-remainder/probes/distance-postedit.txt:3`).+}
