{+After climb batch 7's rung H (`952892a00`; `compile-ladder/rung-exclusion-remainder/REPORT.md` sections 8 and 9): the count stage reads 44, the `FortressLibrary` api stopping at its hierarchy pass on one error, `AnyIntegral`'s `comprises` clause; the distance stage under the setting `any` reads 1,661, from 1,747: exclusion 38 to 0, overloading 502 to 486, return type 91 to 64, body errors 980 to 975, the api 178 to 148, the component 842 to 786. With the `AnyIntegral` error also cleared, on a copy with the keep-the-rule sketch's shape, the count stage reads 190: the api's 147 overloading and return-type errors, 145 already in the distance stage's table and 2 that the base's false exclusions hid from every stage, `SQCAP` between `Maybe`'s and `Just`'s declarations and `isLeftZero` in `LexicographicReduction` (`compile-ladder/rung-exclusion-remainder/probes/cleared/unmask-cleared.txt`). Two distance runs on one unchanged library differed by 2 and 2 errors, big operators' bodies; after the edit the array bodies' joins at `fill` call sites also move between runs, the family's size staying at 19 to 20 (`compile-ladder/rung-exclusion-remainder/probes/distance-variation-base.txt`, `distance-variation-post.txt`). *Climb batch 7 rung A alone (`f3b62bc83`): 1,747 to 1,434 under the setting `any`, with `fill`'s classes A1 (244) and A2 (58) at 0. Two runs of the stage on the untouched base read 1,747 and 1,745 (`compile-ladder/rung-tabulate/probes/distance-base-variation.txt`). They differ in the families this entry names, and also in which `__bigOperatorSugar` bodies are reported as typed at their element and which type a join infers for an array body.*+}
