{+On the flat library no library-only spelling clears the error without changing a walk output (climb batch 7's rung H, `952892a00`; `compile-ladder/rung-exclusion-remainder/REPORT.md` section 6): `Integral[\I\]` without `AnyIntegral` (the keep-the-rule sketch) makes walk refuse C4's check at load, `FlatArrays.fss:26`'s generic `/` against `Integral[\I\]`'s (rung F's decision D4, re-measured; row 341 is the same refusal of C4's `MAX`); `Integral[\I\] ... comprises I`, the compiler library's own idiom (`Library/CompilerAlgebra.fsi:16`, `:24`), passes the checker and overflows walk's exclusion test (row 407); `AnyIntegral` without its clause makes walk refuse the library, the scalar-extension `MAX` against `StandardTotalOrder.MAX`; the ellipsis is refused for an extender the api declares by the specification's `\note` (`Specification/basic/traits.tex:241-246`, which a release build renders as nothing, `Specification/fortress/fortress.tex:35-36`; the rendered text allows `...` in an api's clause, `traits.tex:160-162`, and its `Molecule` example refuses an extender the clause does not list, `:262-279`) and by the checker (row 354); and the team's 2008 clause on `Integral[\I\]` reads 48 on the flat library, the api stopping on five "does not extend Integral[\I\]" errors (`compile-ladder/rung-exclusion-remainder/probes/skeptic/variant-counts.txt:3-30`). The three clearing shapes give one count-stage list. The ways outside the library are the checker accommodation approved and parked on 2026-09-21, which the flattening did not make moot (Scala), or a walk exclusion test that stops at a type variable in a `comprises` clause (Java); the choice is Pavol's (row 459).+}
{+- **The written bound `Object` on the three result-only parameters and row 421's four lines take the distance from 1,747 to 1,337 under `any` and from 1,738 to 1,324 under walk's setting; the comprehension's bound clears nothing** (2026-09-28, climb batch 7 rung B, `de22fd928`; `compile-ladder/rung-result-bounds/`; rows 309, 421, 447, 469-472). `builtinPrimitive[\T extends Object\]`, `fail[\T extends Object\]` and `List`'s nullary `opr BIG <|[\T extends Object\]|>`, api and component, and `StandardMinMax`'s default `MIN` and `MAX` declared `T` (`Library/FortressLibrary.fsi:214-215`, `.fss:266-267`), ten lines. The gate's distance stage, before and after on the tree: N1 340 → 0, N2 24 → 1, R1 32 → 0, R4 18 → 4 under both settings; by site 420 gone and 10 new under `any` (421 and 7 under walk's), the new being `List.fss:322` and `:333`, `ArrayList`'s `fill[\T\]` called with an `ImmutableArray[\E,ZZ32\]`, unmasked by row 421's fix (row 469), and the variation families BR, V2 and O1; the crash rows unchanged; the separate runs on file summed to within 2 of the measured change. Two runs of the stage on the unchanged tree in one worktree agree site for site under both settings (`compile-ladder/rung-result-bounds/probes/distance-AB-any.txt`, `-walk.txt`): the families called the checker's run-to-run variation (BR, V2, O1) do not move between repeated runs of one setup, and do move between setups (all 9 of this rung's new variation sites are shown by distance tables on file before the edit, `compile-ladder/rung-result-bounds/probes/skeptic/three-sites-on-file.txt`) and under edits that touch none of their declarations; a BR error is the checker comparing a unary big operator's body with its nullary sibling's declared type (`opr BIG MINNUM(g)` at `Library/FortressLibrary.fss:3233`, declared `RR64` at `.fsi:1937`, reported against `BigReduction[\RR64,RR64\]`, the nullary's). N2's one site left besides the tuple comparisons, `List.fss:150`, stays refused with a new message ("BottomType->CovariantCollection.AnyCovColl is not applicable", class GB): the comprehension's bound moves it and clears no error. The checker binds a result-only parameter bounded by `Object` to `BOTTOM` (`scala_src/typechecker/Formula.scala:524-527`) and leaves one bounded by `Any` open (`:493`); a program against the one library then has row 421's `a MIN b` accepted at its type and `fail` typed at every context, while a comprehension with its element type unwritten is refused before and after and one with it written, at a tuple or an arrow included, is accepted before and after (`compile-ladder/rung-result-bounds/probes/compcheck/`). The compiled checker checks no static argument written at a call against its bound (`n[\String\]` for `n[\T extends Number\]` accepted; a type application `Box[\(ZZ32, ZZ32)\]` and an inferred argument are refused; row 470), so the written `Object` refuses no written tuple element type today, though rule T-Invk (`Specification/appendices/calculi/basic/static.tex:190-201`) would, and would refuse the library's own unary `opr BIG <|[\T\] g:Generator[\T\]|>` too, which passes its `Any`-bounded `T` as the written static argument of the nullary (`Library/List.fss:179-180`; `compile-ladder/rung-result-bounds/probes/skeptic/SkNullaryVar.edit.check.txt`). Walk reads none of the three bounds: a native's body is matched by its text (`interpreter/glue/NativeApp.java:163-190`) and a result-only parameter meets no argument; a written `Object` on a parameter an argument fixes refuses a tuple, `()` or an arrow with an `InterpreterBug` (row 471). No walk output changed over the 418 interpreter tests (401 the same, 17 unstable as before), both microGPT checks 40 of 40 with identical values, the checker count 62 unchanged. Outside the stage's twelve components, over `ReflectiveQuickCheck`, `QuickCheck` and `Generator22D`: 376 → 365, every new error unmasked, and `QuickCheck.checkResult` (`Library/QuickCheck.fss:1064-1141`) newly reaches the checker's "Not in the trait table: GeneratorZZ32" crash once row 421's `MAX` types its loop range. The failure mode, measured by the skeptic: the written bound turns the checker's "not inferred" error at 362 sites into `T := BottomType`; on the compiled path a call of such a result-only parameter in a value position of a concrete type, its static argument unwritten, compiles and fails JVM verification at load, "VerifyError: Bad return type", and runs with the argument written; the compiler library's `fail(s: String): Zilch` runs compiled in the same position, but a declared `Zilch` is an `InterpreterBug` under walk and the specification forbids writing `BottomType` (`Specification/basic/types-vals-vars.tex:514-515`). So the one library's `fail` meets row 447 at the switch-over, at every value-position call (`compile-ladder/rung-result-bounds/probes/skeptic/SkStopLocal.diff.txt`, `SkStopWritten.diff.txt`, `SkZilchFail.diff.txt`, `SkZilchLocal.diff.txt`).+}
{+- **The compiled checker does not narrow a `typecase` variable in the shorthand form, and neither path accepts the binding form `typecase x = e of`; the clause-binding form `x:T =>` checks in the compiled checker and runs under walk, but the compiled run cannot read its binding; and a type ascription fixes a bare generic call that a branch types at `BottomType`** (2026-09-27, climb batch 7's rung H, `952892a00`; `compile-ladder/rung-exclusion-remainder/probes/typecase/typecase-forms.txt`, each probe type-checked in the compiler's own world and run under walk). `typecase c of Rel[\E\] => useRel[\E\](c)` is refused, "not applicable to an argument of type Cond", on a trait type and on an arrow type (`TcTrait.fss`, `TcNested.fss`), while walk runs both; the specification narrows the variable within the clause (`Specification/basic/expressions/typecase.tex:126-133`). `typecase rp = p of` and `typecase (rp, rq) = (p, q) of` are refused on both paths, "Variable rp is not defined" (`TcBind.fss`, `TcTuple.fss`), against the grammar and its prose (`typecase.tex:55-62`, `:88-93`). The section's note has marked that text for revision since the Working Draft (`typecase.tex:15`), and the implementers replaced it with `typecase Expr of` and a per-clause `Id :` (`ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/parser/DelimitedExpr.rats:122`, `ProjectFortress/astgen/Fortress.ast:594-607`). The specification is therefore unfinished on the form, and its home is the probe and row 460, not an `XXX` test (climb batch 7's judge, `compile-ladder/climb-batch-7/JUDGE-review.md`, finding 2). The clause-binding form `rp:T =>`, the library's own in `cast` (`Library/FortressLibrary.fss:33-37`) and now in `andCondCombine` (`:4558-4566`), checks in the compiled checker and runs under walk (`TcClause.fss`), but on the compiled path the code generator cannot read the binding (row 351): the skeptic's `SkTcBind` compiles and its run dies with `NoClassDefFoundError` (`compile-ladder/rung-exclusion-remainder/pro